  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Construct an N×MN \\times MN×M matrix with entries having **positive** integers such that:\n\n\nIf M&gt;1M \\gt 1M&gt;1, ithi^{th}ith row is **strictly** increasing from left to right with a fixed common difference did_idi​ for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\nIf N&gt;1N \\gt 1N&gt;1, jthj^{th}jth column is **strictly** increasing from top to bottom with a fixed common difference cjc_jcj​ for all 1≤j≤M1\\le j \\le M1≤j≤M.\n**All** the common differences should be **distinct**.\nIn the case of multiple answers, find an arrangement that minimizes the **maximum** element of the matrix.\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains a single line of input, two space-separated integers NNN and MMM - the dimensions of the matrix.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN lines with each line having MMM space-separated integers representing the answer.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N,M≤1051 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^51≤N,M≤105",
      "Sum N⋅MN \\cdot MN⋅M over all cases is atmost 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 3\n1 2\n1 1",
        "output": "1 2 3\n3 6 9\n5 10 15\n1 2\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The values d1,d2,d_1, d_2,d1​,d2​, and d3d_3d3​ are 1,3,1, 3,1,3, and 555 respectively. The values c1,c2,c_1, c_2,c1​,c2​, and c3c_3c3​ are 2,4,2, 4,2,4, and 666 respectively. Note that all these common differences {d1,d2,d3,c1,c2,c3}\\{d_1, d_2, d_3, c_1, c_2, c_3\\}{d1​,d2​,d3​,c1​,c2​,c3​} are distinct. Moreover, it can be shown that over all valid matrices, 151515 is the minimal value of the maximum element of the matrix one can achieve.\nTest case 222: The values d1d_1d1​ is 111. It can be shown that over all valid matrices, 222 is the minimal value of the maximum element of the matrix one can achieve."
      }
    ]
  },
